  <!-- HOW XHAVIC WORKS — accordion steps                          -->
  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="l3-how">
    <div class="l3-how__container">
      <div class="l3-how__header" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="l3-how__heading">How Xhavic Works</h2>
        <p class="l3-how__sub">Xhavic is built on optimistic rollup architecture. Transactions are processed off-chain by the Xhavic network and periodically submitted to Ethereum for final settlement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="l3-how__body">
        <div class="l3-how__steps" id="l3HowSteps" data-reveal-stagger>
          <!-- Step 1 -->
          <details class="l3-how__step" open data-panel="0">
            <summary class="l3-how__stepHead">
              <span class="l3-how__stepNum">01</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepTitle">Submit a Transaction</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepToggle"></span>
            </summary>
            <p class="l3-how__stepBody">Users send transactions from any EVM wallet — MetaMask, WalletConnect, or Xhavic's native dual-wallet interface. The Instant Wallet processes DeFi trades in under 200ms; the Secure Wallet holds high-value transfers in a 24-hour escrow window for reversibility.</p>
          </details>
          <!-- Step 2 -->
          <details class="l3-how__step" data-panel="1">
            <summary class="l3-how__stepHead">
              <span class="l3-how__stepNum">02</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepTitle">Sequence & Execute</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepToggle"></span>
            </summary>
            <p class="l3-how__stepBody">Xhavic's sequencer orders transactions, executes them on a fully EVM-compatible runtime, then batches hundreds of operations into compressed state diffs — achieving 2,000+ TPS at approximately $0.04 per transaction.</p>
          </details>
          <!-- Step 3 -->
          <details class="l3-how__step" data-panel="2">
            <summary class="l3-how__stepHead">
              <span class="l3-how__stepNum">03</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepTitle">Post to Ethereum</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepToggle"></span>
            </summary>
            <p class="l3-how__stepBody">State commitments are posted to Ethereum L1 with a 7-day fraud proof window. Any observer can challenge an invalid state root. The protocol's native data oracle provides tamper-proof price feeds directly at precompile addresses.</p>
          </details>
          <!-- Step 4 -->
          <details class="l3-how__step" data-panel="3">
            <summary class="l3-how__stepHead">
              <span class="l3-how__stepNum">04</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepTitle">Bridge, Automate & Scale</span>
              <span class="l3-how__stepToggle"></span>
            </summary>
            <p class="l3-how__stepBody">Cross-chain bridges move assets between Ethereum and Xhavic with fraud-proof security. AI agents monitor on-chain conditions and trigger automated strategies — trades, rebalancing, liquidation protection — all executing on L2 at L1 security.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
